+
+## Local immutable-release extension
+
+The optional `local` tracker maps a Taskboard release ID to the scheduler issue ID.
+Read APIs include ready and non-ready states; transport failure remains an error.
+Dispatch requires an immutable execution snapshot and a project-scoped atomic claim
+before workspace preparation or task-related app-server creation. The same release
+has at most one attempt and one launch guard, with durable checkout exclusion.
+Local omits workspace hooks, provider-native tools, retry/continuation relaunch and
+workspace deletion. A running, claimed Local release is retained for reconciliation
+even though it is no longer a fresh dispatch candidate.
+
+The Local supervisor freezes each process's model/effort and verifies the actual
+executable capability receipt, input hashes and optional Git baseline before spawn.
+It records a separate process group and observed descendant identities. Result
+receipts do not imply process termination: only verified absence of wrapper, group
+and observed descendants permits a stopped receipt and releases durable occupancy.
+Uncertainty, PID reuse and unavailable result delivery preserve the attempt; recovery
+only replays immutable receipts and never starts another Worker. Local workspaces
+and artifacts are retained. These provider-specific rules do not alter the existing
+issue trackers' lifecycle described above.
+
+Local context also freezes protected Taskboard state paths and the input root. The
+runner adds its own state, workflow and original Todo; the supervisor protects the
+effective Codex home without copying authentication. A native per-process permission
+profile restricts Codex-managed tool writes to the workspace, makes inputs read-only
+and denies private state reads. The controller/app-server remain trusted. Inherited
+MCP, plugins and unneeded tool surfaces are disabled and verified in the effective
+configuration. Local thread/turn requests explicitly select the verified profile,
+never legacy sandbox fields; ineffective/unknown permissions fail before a model
+turn. This extension does not claim a filesystem read allowlist for the whole host.
