 ## License
 
 This project is licensed under the [Apache License 2.0](../LICENSE).
+
+### Local Taskboard releases (optional local extension)
+
+`tracker.kind: local` polls immutable releases from a protected loopback Taskboard
+service. Provider settings require `url`, `project_id`, `instance_id`, `token_env`,
+`state_root`, `supervisor`, `python`, and `capability_file`. Use active states
+`[ready, running]` and terminal states `[in_review, failed, canceled, superseded]`.
+No provider-native issue tools are advertised. Hooks and SSH workers are rejected
+for this provider; the owner prepares workspaces and read-only input snapshots.
+
+Each release is claimed before task-related writes or app-server creation. Per-package
+model/effort are consumed as child-process configuration. One durable launch guard
+prevents relaunch after exit, stall or restart; workspaces and artifacts are retained.
+Result and process-stop receipts are independent. Unknown process state retains its
+checkout occupancy. An observed result is not user acceptance. Other providers keep
+their existing retry and cleanup behavior. The optional Taskboard integration bundle
+contains the supervisor, protected launcher, full configuration example and controlled
+process tests; it is configured explicitly and never installed automatically.
+
+Local also requires the verified native Codex permission-profile protocol. The
+trusted app-server applies a process-only profile to managed tools; private runtime
+state, original Todo and Codex home are denied, while frozen inputs are read-only.
+Inherited MCP/plugins and unneeded optional tools are disabled and checked before
+turn creation. Thread and turn requests select the profile explicitly, omitting
+legacy sandbox fields. Unsupported or changed permissions fail closed; global
+configuration and other tracker sessions are unchanged.
